\draw[->,thick] (A) -- (B) node[midway,above] {$5$};
\draw[->,thick] (O) -- (B) node[midway,right] {$13$};
\draw[dashed,->] (A) -- (0,16) node[above] {$N$};
\draw (0,4) arc[start angle=90,end angle=67.38,radius=4];
\path (1.2,5.5) node {$\theta$};
\path (O) node[below] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}\text{Speed}&=\sqrt{5^2+12^2}\\&=13\text{ km/h}\end{aligned}$

The ground velocity points north-east. Its angle east of north is its bearing.

$\begin{aligned}\tan\theta&=\frac{5}{12}\\\theta&\approx22.62^{\circ}\end{aligned}$

The bearing is $023^{\circ}$ to the nearest degree.

$\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{ground}}=\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{air}}+\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{wind}}$.

$\begin{aligned}\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{air}}&=\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{ground}}-\underset{\sim}{v}_{\text{wind}}\\&=\begin{pmatrix}0\\280\end{pmatrix}-\begin{pmatrix}30\\-40\end{pmatrix}\\&=\begin{pmatrix}-30\\320\end{pmatrix}\text{ km/h}\end{aligned}$

