Take $\underset{\sim}{i}$ east and $\underset{\sim}{j}$ north. Let the still-water velocity be $a\underset{\sim}{i}+b\underset{\sim}{j}$ km/h.

The bank velocity is $(a+5)\underset{\sim}{i}+b\underset{\sim}{j}$. For travel due north, its east component is zero and $b>0$.

$\begin{aligned}a+5&=0\\a&=-5\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}(-5)^2+b^2&=13^2\\b^2&=144\\b&=12\end{aligned}$

[tikz]
